
# Orquestación de IA y Asistentes Virtuales en Logística 4.0

> **PART 2 | Intelligent Supply Chain Control Tower & Operational Analytics**

## 1. Project Overview

This project develops an automated logistics architecture focused on international supply chain operations, maritime inbound shipments, freight forwarder integration and operational analytics.

The solution uses n8n to orchestrate data from multiple logistics providers, standardize shipment information and generate operational indicators.

## 2. Part 1 – Data Integration & Automation

The first phase focuses on integrating multiple logistics data sources.

**Workflow:**

Schedule Trigger → Google Sheets → Merge → Filter → JavaScript → PostgreSQL

Main capabilities:
- Automated data extraction.
- Integration of multiple logistics providers.
- Data consolidation and standardization.
- JavaScript data transformation.
- Centralized shipment database.
- Automated carrier summaries.

## 3. Part 2 – Intelligent Supply Chain Control Tower

The second phase introduces operational monitoring and logistics analytics through two complementary workflows.

### Workflow A – Carrier Performance Analytics

**Process:**

Schedule Trigger → Google Sheets → Merge → Filter → JavaScript → PostgreSQL → Carrier Performance Report

Key indicators:
- Total shipments.
- Delayed shipments.
- Delay percentage.
- Average waiting time.
- Carrier alerts.
- Supplier performance evaluation.

### Workflow B – Weekly Control Tower

**Process:**

Schedule Trigger → PostgreSQL → Shipment Analysis → Route Matrix → Status Analysis → Weekly Report

Main modules:

| Module | Function |
|---|---|
| Shipment Quantity | Shipment volume monitoring |
| Route Matrix | POL, POD and carrier analysis |
| Route Risk | Average delay classification |
| Shipment Status | Operational status monitoring |
| Weekly Report | Weekly performance indicators |
| Data Storage | PostgreSQL and Google Sheets |

